---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';
---

<Base
  title="Disclaimer — Accuracy, Security and Advice Limits"
  description="Accuracy, security and professional-advice disclaimers for the DevSnap developer tools, and who is responsible for them."
  schemas={{
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'WebPage',
    name: 'Disclaimer — Accuracy, Security and Advice Limits',
    url: `${SITE.domain}/disclaimer/`,
    author: { '@type': 'Person', name: SITE.author },
    publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: SITE.publisher },
  }}
  canonicalPath="/disclaimer/"
>
  <div class="wrap wrap-narrow">
    <ol class="crumbs">
      <li><a href="/">Home</a></li>
      <li>Disclaimer</li>
    </ol>

    <header class="tool-hero">
      <h1>Disclaimer</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        A short, honest statement of what these tools are good for, and what they are
        not good for.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose mt-3">
      <h2>Accuracy</h2>
      <p>
        The tools are implemented against published specifications and tested against
        known values, but they are not infallible. A formatting tool can produce output
        that differs from a particular implementation, a regular expression can behave
        differently across languages, and a date calculation can differ around a
        daylight saving boundary.
      </p>
      <p>
        Always verify output that matters before relying on it, particularly in a
        production system, a security context or a financial one.
      </p>

      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p>
        These tools are provided as they are. The privacy and security properties
        described on this site — that input is processed locally and never
        transmitted — describe the architecture of the site as published. If you
        deploy a copy of these tools yourself, that is your deployment and your
        responsibility.
      </p>
      <p>
        Nothing on this site is a substitute for a proper security review, a
        professional penetration test, or the documentation of the system you are
        working on.
      </p>

      <h2>Not professional advice</h2>
      <p>
        The guides and the notes attached to each tool are general technical
        information. They are not legal, financial, medical or regulatory advice, and
        they are not a substitute for the specific guidance of a qualified
        professional in your jurisdiction.
      </p>
      <p>
        In particular, the tax, payroll and financial examples used to illustrate a
        tool are illustrative only. Do not use them to make a financial or
        compliance decision.
      </p>

      <h2>Trademarks</h2>
      <p>
        Product names, logos and trademarks referenced in the documentation belong to
        their respective owners and are used for identification only. Mentioning a
        product does not imply endorsement.
      </p>

      <h2>External links</h2>
      <p>
        Links to other sites are provided for convenience. We are not responsible for
        the content or practices of third-party sites.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        If something here is wrong, <a href="/contact/">tell us</a> at
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
